💭 Calls that are made directly instead of through a dispatch table, and 🤯, which the compiler knows never returns.

🐇 🐭 🚧 🍇
  🆕 🍇
    ⤴️🆕 🔤squeak🔤❗️
  🍉
🍉

🕊 🧰 🍇
  🆕 🍇🍉

  💭 A function with a return type may end with 🤯.
  🐇❗️ 🔍 n 🔢 ➡️ 🔢 🍇
    ↪️ n ▶️🙌 0 🍇
      ↩️ n ✖️ 2
    🍉
    🤯🐇💻 🔤negative🔤❗️
  🍉

  💭 🤯 ends a branch as ↩️ does, so this returns on all paths.
  🐇❗️ 🔎 n 🔢 ➡️ 🔡 🍇
    ↪️ n 🙌 1 🍇
      ↩️ 🔤one🔤
    🍉
    🙅↪️ n 🙌 2 🍇
      ↩️ 🔤two🔤
    🍉
    🙅 🍇
      🤯🐇💻 🔤too large🔤❗️
    🍉
  🍉

  💭 🚧 is exported and has subclasses, but 💬 is 🔏.
  🐇❗️ 💌 error 🚧 ➡️ 🔡 🍇
    ↩️ 💬error❗️
  🍉
🍉

